{"section": "unified_entries", "ordinal_zero_based": 62536, "record": {"tibetan": "ལས་ཀྱི་དབང", "wylie": "las kyi dbang", "wylie_variants": ["las kyi dbang"], "tenses": null, "sanskrit": "{LC}karmavaśitā; {LC}karmavaśa", "hopkins_english": null, "hgm_gloss": null, "hgm_evidence": null, "status": "awaiting-hgm-equivalent", "acip": "LAS KYI DBANG", "lc_source": ["main", "supplement-1992"], "lc_refs": ["{sc19}8o", "{sc52}79.14"], "pronunciation": "le kyi wang", "scaffold_added": "lc-v27", "corpus_occurrences": {"courses": ["C03", "C05", "C08", "C09", "C12", "C15", "C16", "C17", "C18", "EM", "GIE", "ILL", "P1", "P7"], "n_segments": 43}, "attestation_contexts": [{"course": "C03", "tibetan_wylie": "'dis rang cag rnams sngon chad thob med nas da bar sdug bsngal mi bzad pa la sbyar zhing , da dung nyon mongs 'di gtan brlag tu gtong thub pa zhig ma byung na, de'i dbang gis las bsags, las kyi dbang gis 'khor ba'i gnas ", "hgm_english": "From time with no beginning up to the present moment, this enemy has led us by the hand to all kinds of unbearable pain. And if still we find ourselves unable to discard these bad thoughts once and for all, they will force us to collect karma. Then the karma w"}, {"course": "C05", "tibetan_wylie": "ji skad du, sems can las kyi dbang gis ri, , nag po'i dus su skyes te dper, , sems dmyal mtho ris 'jig rten du, , mtshon dang rin chen shing bzhin no, , zhes gsungs so, , 'jig rten gnyis thun mong gi las yin min gnyis ky", "hgm_english": "As the verse goes, It's through the karma of living beings That the great dark mountains arise in their time. It's like the hells, and the heavens above, And swords, and jewels, and trees in the world. The great books of the Mind-Only School also discuss wheth"}], "tibetan_source": "generated-ewts-v27-1"}}
